// Inverse kinematics on the test rig standing on a 20 degree slope, from its graph's IK (the
// Animator tab's IK: Assets/LegsIk.fgraph). Foot IK (weight from the graph's Feet parameter, saved
// for _reload) puts each foot on the slope under it in Play, one up and one down (the editor's own
// colliders are bodies in Play only: in edit mode the feet find the terrain and cooked ones); the
// Animator's Feet 0, and a script's weight 0, leave the clip's feet (level). Entity parameters
// (LookTarget, AimTarget, AimHold, HandTarget) bound in the Animator, in edit mode and again after
// Stop: the head looks at an Empty and follows it as it moves, the left hand aims at one, reaches
// one, then is held at one (pointing where it faces, turning with it; the spine turning with it,
// or with "spine": 0 the arms alone, the shoulder where the clip has it); itself is refused; one is
// bound with the Inspector's pick button and a click in the Hierarchy. Deleting a bound entity
// clears the binding (Undo brings both back). Script API v12: the head looks at a point (the spine
// and neck turning with it), the left hand reaches one; an unknown bone is refused. v13: the left
// hand aims at a point (the spine turning, the head looking there too), ahead as posed or along an
// axis of its own (along the arm), or held at a point while it aims; a bone with no spine above it
// is refused. v14: Physics.Raycast down onto the slope. v16: Animation.SetEntity / GetEntity /
// ResetEntity (a script's binding over the Animator's, gone at Stop; an unknown parameter refused).
